From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: stop asking the JPEG encoder to rotate -- it cannot

needJpegRotation() returned true unconditionally, which broke every still capture.
The hardware JPEG encoder does not implement rotation:

  mm-still: QImageHW10Encoder::IsAvailable(): wont support rotation
  mm-still: QImageHW10Encoder::New(): validation failed

so requesting it disqualified the hardware encoder and fell back to software, which
mishandles it: the saved JPEG came out with the sensor's dimensions transposed
(a 4160x3120 stream stored as 3120x4160) with the frame data repeated in bands,
while the preview -- never rotated -- was perfectly correct.

It was also redundant. CAM_QCOM_FEATURE_PP_SUPERSET_HAL3 already includes
CAM_QCOM_FEATURE_ROTATION and the CPP acts on it.
---
 camera/QCamera2/HAL3/QCamera3HWI.cpp | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/camera/QCamera2/HAL3/QCamera3HWI.cpp b/camera/QCamera2/HAL3/QCamera3HWI.cpp
index 4eb494a..ccac2ca 100644
--- a/camera/QCamera2/HAL3/QCamera3HWI.cpp
+++ b/camera/QCamera2/HAL3/QCamera3HWI.cpp
@@ -7694,7 +7694,38 @@ bool QCamera3HardwareInterface::needReprocess(uint32_t postprocess_mask)
  *==========================================================================*/
 bool QCamera3HardwareInterface::needJpegRotation()
 {
-    return true;
+    /* Only ask the JPEG encoder to rotate if the post-processor cannot do it.
+     *
+     * This used to return true unconditionally, which broke every still
+     * capture on ether. The hardware JPEG encoder does not implement rotation:
+     *
+     *   mm-still: QImageHW10Encoder::IsAvailable(): wont support rotation
+     *   mm-still: QImageHW10Encoder::New(): validation failed
+     *   mm-still: preloadCodecLibs(): Use SW_CODEC_ONLY flag true
+     *
+     * so requesting rotation disqualified the hardware encoder and fell back to
+     * software, which mishandles it: the saved JPEG came out with the sensor's
+     * dimensions transposed (4160x3120 stream stored as 3120x4160) and the
+     * frame data repeated in bands, while the preview -- which is never rotated
+     * -- was perfectly correct.
+     *
+     * It was also redundant. CAM_QCOM_FEATURE_PP_SUPERSET_HAL3 includes
+     * CAM_QCOM_FEATURE_ROTATION and is applied to the postprocess mask, and the
+     * CPP really does act on it:
+     *
+     *   mm-camera: pproc_module_send_set_param_event: rotation:8, strmId:5
+     *
+     * So the frame was already being rotated upstream. The !needJpegRotation
+     * branches in QCamera3PostProc swap the source and destination dimensions
+     * to match exactly that case.
+     *
+     * Gate on the capability rather than hardcoding, matching upstream CAF.
+     */
+    if (!(gCamCapability[mCameraId]->qcom_supported_feature_mask &
+            CAM_QCOM_FEATURE_ROTATION)) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    return false;
 }
 
